se_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%27%C3%AAn_Fang-chi\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;\u00ean Fang-chi\">Ch'\u00ean Fang-chi</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367037\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367037\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3633519</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Ch&#39;\u00ean Chuan</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Fang Chao-ying</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"85\" data-page-number=\"85\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/97\" data-page-index=\"97\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/97\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;97\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>CH'\u00caN</b> Chuan \u9673\u64b0 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u695e\u5c71,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u7389\u51e0), poet and artist, was a native of Hangchow who lived late in the seventeenth and early in the eighteenth centuries, or approximately from 1670 to 1740. His family came originally from Ningpo, and he himself studied under the eminent scholar, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Mao_Ch%27i-ling\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Mao Ch&#39;i-ling\">Mao Ch'i-ling</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. Though he achieved fame as a poet and a painter, he lived most of the time in seclusion and had few friends. In the second and third decades of the eighteenth century he lived in Yangchow as the guest of a rich merchant.\n</p><p>The collected poems of Ch'\u00ean Chuan, entitled \u7389\u51e0\u5c71\u623f\u541f\u5377 <i>Y\u00fc-chi shan-fang yin-ch\u00fcan</i>, 3 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, were printed about the years 1716-21. In 1735 he was recommended to take the second special <i>po-hs\u00fceh hung-tz'\u016d</i> examination of 1736, but politely declined. Friends of his who did take the examination were <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Li_%C3%8A\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Li \u00ca\">Li \u00ca</a></span> and <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Hang_Shih-ch%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Hang Shih-ch\u00fcn\">Hang Shih-ch\u00fcn</a></span>&#32;[<i>qq.&#8239;v.</i>], the latter having left an account of Ch'\u00ean's life. Three of Ch'\u00ean's paintings are listed in the \u750c\u9262\u7f85\u5ba4\u66f8\u756b\u904e\u76ee\u8003 <i>Ou-po-lo-shih shu-hua kuo-mu k'ao</i> (1894) by Li Y\u00fc-f\u00ean (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Wang_Shih-min\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Wang Shih-min\">Wang Shih-min</a></span>); and a volume of miscellaneous notes by him concerning famous men&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"86\" data-page-number=\"86\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/98\" data-page-index=\"98\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/98\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;98\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>of Hangchow was printed in the second series of the <i>Ku-hs\u00fceh hui-k'an</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Li_Ch%27ing\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Li Ch&#39;ing\">Li Ch'ing</a></span>).\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/490/2b; 3/433/15a; 26/1/35a; 29/4/20a; 31/4/24a; <i>Y\u00fc-chi shan-fang yin-ch\u00fcan</i>, reprinted in \u56db\u660e\u53e2\u66f8 <i>Ss\u016d ming ts'ung-shu</i>, fourth series (1934).]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Fang Chao-ying</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean Ch'i-y\u00fcan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean Fang-chi"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Hang Shih-ch\u00fcn"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Li Ch'ing"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Li \u00ca"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Mao Ch'i-ling"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wang Shih-min"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Fang Chao-ying"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = ch'en chuan\n | previous = Ch'\u00ean Ch'i-y\u00fcan\n | next     = Ch'\u00ean Fang-chi\n | from     = 97\n | to       = 98\n | notes    = \n | section_author = Fang Chao-ying\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Ch'\u00ean Chuan}}"}}}